12:15:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mineral, CO; Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6ed6bf45cfd2c9b7e2914c85b381b2ff9ad5afc7.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6ed6bf45cfd2c9b7e2914c85b381b2ff9ad5afc7.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 7:12PM MDT until October 24 at 10:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"...The Flood Warning is extended for the following rivers in\nColorado...\n\nRio Grande Near Del Norte affecting Rio Grande County.\n\n.High flows and flooding will continue along the Rio Grande through\nDel Norte.  The river levels will continue to fall but remain in\nminor flood stage into Saturday morning.\n\nFor the Upper Rio Grande River...including Del Norte...Minor flooding\nis forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Rio Grande  near Del Norte.\n\n* WHEN...Until Saturday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 6.5 feet, Moderate Flood. Water flows over low spots\nin Hanna Lane Road west of Del Norte. Water threatens homes and RV\npark near Del Norte Park in Del Norte. Homes near First Street and\nthe Oak Street Bridge on Colorado Highway 112 are threatened by\nhigh water.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 6:46 PM MDT Friday the stage was 6.4 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 5.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 6:46 PM MDT Friday was 6.6 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage late\ntomorrow morning and continue falling to 3.2 feet Wednesday\nevening.\n- Flood stage is 5.5 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 6.4\nfeet on 06/29/1927.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-24T22:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2278d6564e523f4ffadf9b13c28ddb6dc7687afe.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2278d6564e523f4ffadf9b13c28ddb